==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|iule}}, {{m|gmh|iuwel}}, from {{inh|de|goh|ūwila}}, from a variant of {{inh|de|gem-pro|*uwwalǭ}} (compare {{cog|nl|uil}}, {{cog|fy|ûle}}, {{cog|en|owl}}), diminutive of {{m|gem-pro|*uwwǭ}} ‘eagle-owl’ (compare {{cog|de|Uhu}}), of {{onomatopoeic|de|title=imitative}} origin or a variant of {{m|gem-pro|*ūfaz}}, {{m|gem-pro|*ūfǭ}} (compare {{cog|sv|uv}} ‘horned owl’, Bavarian {{m|bav|Auf}}), from {{der|de|ine-pro|*up-}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˈʔɔɪ̯lə/}}
* {{audio|de|De-Eule.ogg}}
* {{rhymes|de|ɔɪ̯lə|s=2}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|f|dim=chen}}

# [[owl]]
# a [[moth]] of the family {{taxfmt|Noctuidae|family}}
# {{lb|de|chronobiology}} a [[human]] who [[go to bed|goes to bed]] [[late]] and [[rise]]s late, a [[night owl]]
